Commissioner ho can you met this morning  here in Washington DC with the  counterparts from the United States and  Japan I understand that there is an  agreement to strengthen existing rules  on industrial subsidies and condemn  forced technology transfer practices can  you tell us a little bit more about this  well I'm very pleased that the European  Union the United States and Japan are  able to come to an agreement in respect  of our statement of intent to deal with  industrial subsidies and forced  technology transfer because we need a  level playing field for all of our  companies in order to be able to trade  locally and regrettably we don't have  this restricted level playing field  presently some countries are flowering  the rules and disciplines that are in  the WTO process at the moment so we have  to revise our rules to take account of  the fact that the WTO rules have not  been changed for 25 years and we have to  adapt those rules to the modern  industrial and trading environment that  we have at the moment so ambassador  light hyzer and minister kagiyama from  japan and myself were very pleased to be  able to advance this work and build on  the progress that was made by the  Minister for Trade mentor Sachi and  Commissioner Malmstrom over the last  number of months Commission you have a  very busy schedule here in Washington DC  these days and you'll be meeting with  members of Congress and meaning a  meeting with members of the US  administration what is your message to  the Americans well I want to see the  United States and European Union  resetting its relationship and to  developing a positive and common trade  agenda we have an enormous amount of  work to do we agree on many things but  we haven't really developed a structural  dialogue in relation to these issues in  a positive way in the last number of  years so I hope that ambassador  lighthouse or an i and other  interlocutors that we'll be meeting in  the United States here this week will be  able to agree with us that we have more  in common and then perhaps we realize  and that we want to engage in  cooperation and dialogue rather than in  confrontation in relation to matters  that are before us and in dispute at the  moment so we setting and refreshing the  relationship and developing a positive  agenda around trade is the objective of  the visit  great Thank You commissioner
 

